     "2018-04-26 16:15 GMT+02:00 Paul &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">guey...@gmail.com</a>&gt;:\r<br>&gt; patient &lt;-  trajectory(&quot;patients&#39; path&quot;) %&gt;%\r<br>&gt;   branch(option = function()\r<br>&gt; sample(1:3,1,prob=c(0.1,0.2,0.7)),continue=c(T,T,F),\r<br>&gt;          trajectory()%&gt;%\r<br>&gt;            seize(&quot;admit&quot;,1)%&gt;%\r<br>&gt;            timeout(function() runif(1,15,20))%&gt;%\r<br>&gt;            release(&quot;admit&quot;,1),\r<br>&gt;          trajectory()%&gt;%\r<br>&gt;            seize(&quot;tests&quot;,1)%&gt;%\r<br>&gt;            timeout(function() runif(1,15,20))%&gt;%\r<br>&gt;            release(&quot;tests&quot;,1)%&gt;%\r<br>&gt;            rollback(amount=6,times=1),\r<br>\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "Note that amount=4 would be enough: &gt; release &gt; timeout &gt; seize &gt; branch.\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "\r<br>&gt;          trajectory()%&gt;%\r<br>&gt;            seize(&quot;discharge&quot;)%&gt;%\r<br>&gt;            timeout(function() 0)%&gt;%\r<br>&gt;            release(&quot;discharge&quot;)\r<br>&gt;          )%&gt;%\r<br>&gt;   seize(&quot;discharge&quot;)%&gt;%\r<br>&gt;   timeout(function() 0)%&gt;%\r<br>&gt;   release(&quot;discharge&quot;)\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; I&#39;ve got the following trajectory for a patient who can be admitted or sent\r<br>&gt; for tests or discharged. what i need is the patients going for tests to come\r<br>&gt; back and go to either admitted or discharged\r<br>\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "This trajectory allows a patient to be sent for tests more than once,\r<br>because you are exposing them to the branch decision more than once.\r<br>Is that what you want?\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "\r<br>&gt; However, when i run it with\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; env2 &lt;- simmer(&quot;patientpathway&quot;)%&gt;%\r<br>&gt;   add_resource(&quot;admit&quot;,2)%&gt;%\r<br>&gt;   add_resource(&quot;tests&quot;,3)%&gt;%\r<br>&gt;   add_resource(&quot;discharge&quot;,3)%&gt;%\r<br>&gt;   add_generator(&quot;patient&quot;, patient,function(){rpois(1,5)},mon=2)%&gt;%\r<br>&gt;   run(1000)\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; arrivals &lt;- get_mon_arrivals(env2,per_resource=TRUE)\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; and look at the arrivals, some of the patients are going for tests and then\r<br>&gt; disappearing, which isn&#39;t what I want and I can&#39;t figure out where I&#39;m going\r<br>&gt; wrong.\r<br>\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "Note that times=1. Therefore, those patients who are entering the\r<br>tests trajectory for a second time don&#39;t rollback. These are your\r<br>&quot;disappearing&quot; arrivals.\r<br>"
